---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Cory Simenson">
  <Header />

  <main style="max-width: 760px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem;">
    <h1>About Me</h1>

    <section style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <h2>Who I Am</h2>
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">
        I’m Cory Simenson — a Linux-focused systems builder working across automation,
        virtualization, home infrastructure, and long-term creative engineering. My work
        blends practical problem-solving with structured, operator-style workflows that
        emphasize clarity, stability, and repeatability.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <h2>What I Work On</h2>
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">
        I build and maintain systems across KVM/QEMU virtualization, Home Assistant
        automation, Linux networking, and multi-machine development environments. My
        projects often involve designing stable home infrastructure, optimizing hardware,
        and creating tools that reduce friction in daily workflows.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <h2>Current Focus</h2>
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">
        I’m currently developing a unified digital portfolio, transitioning my smart home
        ecosystem to Home Assistant Supervisor, and refining multi-room home stability
        workflows. I also maintain several Linux systems — Zora, Pavilion, and Victus —
        each with dedicated roles in my automation and development environment.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <h2>Trajectory</h2>
      <p style="line-height: 1.6;">
        My long-term trajectory includes deepening my systems engineering practice,
        expanding my automation stack, and continuing my migration and citizenship
        planning work. I approach each project with a focus on reliability, clarity, and
        long-term maintainability.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
